I'm a thoroughly spoiled player with 6 or 7 ascensions under my
belt--mostly priests, 1 valkyrie and 1 tourist. I've been playing
nothing but monks lately, and I guess I finally figured them out.
This is my first time to finish the monk quest. I just used the
same trick as with other quests: free action plus wielded paralysis.
Then I discovered how *awesome* the Eyes are. They make light
obsolete, and Gehennom bearable.

I've found the vibrating square and left the bell and candelabrum
there. Now I've kind of been hanging around, not quite confident
enough to wake Rodney. I got up to XL 15 without succubi or
potions, and then drank 2 potions just to get the teleport control.
With a bit of nurse dancing I'm up to 290 HP. My AC is -33 with
my +5 robe on, -32 with the +4 cloak of magic resistance. I really
want to do the monk roleplay, so no body armor or shield. I'm still
vegan, and it should be trivial to maintain that. I'm also staying
celibate; no succubi. Even though I broke weaponless conduct
with a pickaxe accident when I first arrived on the Medusa level,
I'm pretending I'm still weaponless. I would also like to ascend
with my pet green dragon; I've always ascended petless.
Oh yeah, I have 1 wish left, and I don't wish for artifacts. So I
know, these are several artificial restrictions to put on myself,
but I'd really like to ascend my first monk this way. But can I?

Obviously my only source of reflection would be the amulet.
So I have to choose between reflection and life saving. All but
one of my ascensions were reflectionless, but usually I have
super-duper artifact weapons and at least 10 more points of AC.
How much of a difference will reflection make from this point on?

I'm also not sure of the choice between the robe and the cloak.
With all the talk of redundant MR, I guess I should use the cloak.
But I think that will make a big difference in spellcasting.

I'm neutral, and my tourist ascended lawful. I'm very tempted to
wish for the helm of opposite alignment so I only have to make it
to one high altar.

I don't know if I'm looking for advice, or just reassurance that I
can pull this off. I have a lot of the usual equipment, but I don't
know what specific items I should list.



